<title>USA: Teva get okayfor 600 mg Tolemtim Sodium.</title>
<headline>Teva get okayfor 600 mg Tolemtim Sodium.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Teva Pharmaceutical Industries Ltd  said the U.S. Food and Drug Administration has aproved its application to manufacture and market 600-mg. Tolmetin Sodium tablets.</p>
<p>Tolemetin Sodium is a generic equivalent of McNeil's Tolectin 600, a drug for the treatment of arthritis. There are several generic versions of the product and Teva already manufacturers and markets Tolmetin Sodium in 400 mg. capsules, it said.</p>
<p>Teva Pharmaceutical is based in Jerusalem, Israel.</p>
</text>
